    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Late-Tertiary Lake MeadFault System (LMFS) located in the Basin and Range is a major left-lateral fault system that contains areas of regional tectonic subsidence and local uplifts. The Overton Arm basin is a deep pull-apart basin located between a large left-step in the LMFS. The Echo Hills is a distinctive structural domain of shortening contained within a small right-step in a strand of the LMFS. Both features are directly a result of strike-slip motion along the LMFS.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
